omx-contract (3.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 3.0.0: the changelog names the whole major, the hosting codes moved to
    omx-clap-core (#137)
  * data/hosting out: the 16 hosting files leave for omx-clap-core, byte for
    byte (RQ1, #137)
  * docs: the hosting codes are omx-clap-core's,
    contract.d/3/omx-clap-core/hosting/; data/ holds no hosting code (#137)
  * schema major 3: formerly and c.alias deleted, schema 3.0.0, the v3
    $schema URL, hosting floors >= 3.0.0 (#136)
  * docs: schema 3.0.0, formerly and c.alias removed, the v3 $schema URL,
    owners read from contract.d/3/ only (#136)
  * schema: descriptor words extensions, plugin.doc and the ratio unit; the
    formatMap kind (#136)
  * docs/descriptors: the extension bag, the formatMap kind, the ratio unit
    and plugin.doc (#136)
  * #1841 out: the default EQ rule leaves for omx-dsp; the band budget and
    counts are declarative (#136)
  * docs: the checks word and the generic sheet-default rule; the default EQ
    rule leaves for omx-dsp (#1841, #136)
  * data/hosting: each file states its schema floor, requires
    omx-contract-schema >= 2.18.0 (#136)
  * render: --package spells the package's codes and words by kind, as
    omx_vocabulary.h does (#136)
  * docs/render: render --package renders the package's vocabulary, by kind,
    as omx_vocabulary.h spells it (#136)
  * hosting/features: hosting.features.ports-unreadable, a plugin whose
    declared ports the reader cannot read (omx-clap-core#255)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:19:09 +0000
